### Health check
GET http://localhost:8080/health

### 1. Register a new user
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "vaibhav@example.com",
  "password": "vaibhav123"
}

### 2. Login (copy the "token" value from the response for the next requests)
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "vaibhav@example.com",
  "password": "vaibhav123"
}

### 3. Create a ticket (replace YOUR_TOKEN_HERE below with the token from step 2)
POST http://localhost:8080/tickets
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE

{
  "title": "Printer broken",
  "description": "Office printer not working"
}

### 4. List your own tickets
GET http://localhost:8080/tickets
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE

### 5. Get a single ticket by ID (change t1 if needed)
GET http://localhost:8080/tickets/t1
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE

### 6. Update ticket status: open -> in_progress
PATCH http://localhost:8080/tickets/t1/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE

{
  "status": "in_progress"
}

### 7. Update ticket status: in_progress -> closed
PATCH http://localhost:8080/tickets/t1/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE

{
  "status": "closed"
}

### 8. Try to reopen a closed ticket (should fail with 400)
PATCH http://localhost:8080/tickets/t1/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE

{
  "status": "open"
}
